<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 24: </span><span id="A6.T24.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parallel scaling with Chinese as the source language.</span>
All experiments use Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and are evaluated on multilingual
MATH500. Adding the first parallel language yields the largest gain, while
adding a second language provides a smaller additional improvement.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Dataset License</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use publicly available models and benchmarks, including the multilingual versions of MATH500 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, AIME2024, AIME2025 from XReasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and GPQA-Diamond <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rein et al., 2023</a>)</cite> from BenchMAX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and follow their corresponding usage guidelines.</p>
</div>
